sequenceDiagram
    actor User as CLI User
    participant TD as TeardownCommand
    participant EC2 as AWS EC2
    participant S3 as AWS S3
    participant CF as AWS CloudFormation
    participant SSM as AWS SSM
    participant IB as EC2 Image Builder

    Note over User,IB: baas admin teardown -- needs the elevated BaasCliDeployerPolicy.<br/>Deletes the CORE stack, then retires the runner image build-image created outside it.<br/>The CI stack and the results table are untouched.
    User->>TD: baas admin teardown [--stack-name] [--yes] [--delete-bucket]
    Note over TD: ConfigService.load() from ~/.baas/config.yaml<br/>stack = --stack-name, else the configured prefix (the stack IS the prefix)

    rect rgb(255, 235, 235)
        Note over TD,EC2: Gate 1 -- never tear down under a live job
        TD->>EC2: describeInstances(tag baas-role=benchmark-runner, state=pending|running)
        EC2-->>TD: instances, with each one's baas-job-id tag
        alt running runner instances found
            TD-->>User: abort naming each job id (from the tag), instance and state,<br/>and `baas jobs terminate <jobId>` -- exit 1. No table read: the deployer has none
        end
    end

    opt --yes not set
        Note over TD,User: Gate 2 -- explicit confirmation
        alt no terminal to ask on
            TD-->>User: refuse, pass --yes -- exit 1, nothing deleted (U32)
        end
        TD->>User: prompt: type the stack name to confirm deletion
        User-->>TD: typed input
        alt input does not match the stack name exactly
            TD-->>User: "Aborted. Nothing was deleted." exit 1
        end
    end

    TD->>CF: describeStacks -> RunnerImageExtensionData
    CF-->>TD: the deployed extension, or empty
    opt an extension is deployed
        Note over TD: written with its marker to runner-image-extension.<prefix>.yaml<br/>beside the config file -- the stack holds its only copy (U40).<br/>Cannot read or write it -> exit 1, nothing deleted
    end

    alt --delete-bucket set
        TD->>S3: listObjectsV2Paginator(bucket)
        S3-->>TD: object keys (paginated)
        TD->>S3: deleteObject(key) for each object
        TD->>S3: deleteBucket(bucket)
        alt deletion fails
            Note over TD: warn and CONTINUE -- leaving the stack behind is worse<br/>than leaving the bucket behind, and the bucket is recoverable by hand
        end
    else default (bucket retained)
        Note over TD,S3: the bucket survives -- DeletionPolicy Retain means CloudFormation<br/>will not remove it either
    end

    TD->>CF: deleteStack(stackName)
    CF-->>TD: delete accepted
    TD->>CF: waiter.waitUntilStackDeleteComplete()
    loop poll DescribeStacks
        CF-->>TD: status = DELETE_IN_PROGRESS
    end
    CF-->>TD: status = DELETE_COMPLETE

    rect rgb(235, 245, 255)
        Note over TD,IB: Retire the runner image -- always, AFTER the stack (a failed stack deletion keeps an image to run on).<br/>prefix = the deployment torn down (--stack-name), not this machine's. No step fails the teardown.
        TD->>SSM: getParameter(/<prefix>/runner/ami-id)
        opt pointer present and its AMI still exists
            TD->>EC2: describeImages -- collect snapshot ids
            TD->>EC2: deregisterImage(ami), deleteSnapshot(each)
        end
        TD->>SSM: deleteParameter(/<prefix>/runner/ami-id) -- even if the AMI could not be retired
        TD->>IB: listImages(owner Self, name <prefix>-recipe-runner) + listImageBuildVersions
        TD->>IB: deleteImage(each build version)
        alt everything removed
            TD-->>User: "Runner image retired ... needs baas admin build-image before baas run"
        else something failed
            TD-->>User: warn: each leftover, with the aws command that removes it (exit stays 0)
        end
    end

    opt bucket was retained
        TD-->>User: warn: a later `baas admin setup` for this deployment will FAIL while<br/>the bucket exists -- its name derives from the ACCOUNT, so this hits whoever<br/>runs it next, not just you. Delete it by hand or re-run with --delete-bucket.
    end
    Note over TD: name BOTH retained resources -- a setup that trips over one<br/>and then the other is two rounds of the same opaque error
    TD-->>User: "S3 bucket retained" (unless --delete-bucket),<br/>"DynamoDB results table retained -- there is no flag to delete it --<br/>benchmark history outlives the stack" and exit 0
